Collect Haskell query counters under the connection lock even when a
maintenance test already closed the database, then dispose the agent.
Never query a closed C handle to collect this metadata.

Raise the terminal and server-start waits to 30 seconds.  The release test
build runs with debug assertions off, and the full suite on a loaded machine
routinely needs more than the upstream five seconds before the client prints.

Index: tests/ChatClient.hs
